<title>USA: Millennium Chemicals tax rate to increase.</title>
<headline>Millennium Chemicals tax rate to increase.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Millennium Chemicals Inc said Friday its tax rate will increase through this year as tax benefits accruing from its de-merger from Hanson Plc disappear.</p>
<p>The company paid just $17 million in taxes in the 1997 first quarter, compared with a proforma $281 million a year ago.</p>
<p>&quot;The low level of tax in the first quarter will be given back in the course of the next quarters of this year,&quot; Chief Financial Officer John Lushefski told a conference call after the company released its first quarter results.</p>
<p>He said the tax benefits from the de-merger would expire by 1999. &quot;By the year 2000 our tax rate will be 38 percent or so,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>((--David Chance, New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
